{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys","id":1320371,"title":"What if the Setting recognized the Sidhe as the badguys?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-23T18:50:18-07:00","id":1320371,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What if the Setting recognized the Sidhe as the badguys?","content":"So the books really downplay the horror of the Sidhe basically they came back to the world from beyond, stole mortal Bodies and banished their souls to Arcadia. And then they warred and conquered the Fae who remained on Earth.<br /> <br /> Some have even theorized they intended to have the Sidhe as the badguys of the series in the older drafts. So what if we just make that change to the setting? What if we portray the other changelings in a similar situation to other supernaturals, in that they are warring against a rival faction, this case the Sidhe. So the setting would be the Sidhe Commoner war never ended but the Sidhe are winning. The game would be about hiding from the Sidhe, fighting the Sidhe, or coming to terms with the Sidhe.<br /> <br /> In such a game the Sidhe would be more like the more sinister Supernaturals, like Vampires and Demons, while the Changelings are more Neutral like Wraiths and Mages. And werewolves would not be as friendly with the Changelings as in standard games treating Sidhe as Soul Stealers, but other fae would be treated as neutral.<br /> <br /> This give some more goals in the game.<br /> <br /> Maybe Fomorians are just the eldest Fae or like in Dark Age Fae just one camp. Like maybe the Nobles kept the 4 Seasons Seemings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T16:14:00-07:00","id":1320603,"title":"","content":"I can't really say much about the setting in such a scenario, but from a logistical/development standpoint, I think early in the second edition, you'd have seen a Players Guide to the Sidhe (similar to Vampire's original Sabbat book) that would've introduced the Houses, with discussion of how each views commoners. <br /> <br /> Also, the commoner political set up might've been a bit more dynamic than what was presented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T16:59:56-07:00","id":1320610,"title":"","content":"I think that would require you to retcon the entire concept of the Sidhe.<br /> <br /> Remember, Changelings are the living embodiment of mortal dreams. And when it comes to the Sidhe, they embody the dream of nobility, leadership, grace, wisdom, perfection and (most of all) superiority. Sidhe do not merely claim to be better than everybody else, they ARE better than everybody else. They were literally born to rule, and The Dreaming fully supports them in this situation. Once they returned to the world, they demanded their holdings back, and even though the peasants said <i>&quot;no,&quot;</i> The Dreaming said <i>&quot;of course, your majesty!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> In this hypothetical situation, we would have to look to the Autumn Sidhe for answers on how to handle a setting in which the Arcadian Sidhe are the villains. The way I imagine it, the Autumn Sidhe are the only Kith that The Dreaming wouldn't instantly turn against for trying to oppose their Arcadian counterparts. At that point, it becomes a land dispute between nobles, and to the victor goes the spoils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T19:15:46-07:00","id":1320638,"title":"","content":"The Dreaming complied with the Sidhe but it didn't turn on the commoners. The Dreaming after all didn't instantly turn on the commoners during the War, the Sidhe had to first win the war.<br /> <br /> But yes I imagine the Autumn Sidhe would be a big factor, but they would be a minority compared to a conquering Host. But in this Setting the Sidhe might also include the Fomorians.<br /> <br /> Someone else suggested to me maybe the Fomorians could be the mortal souls of the hijacked bodies. Then I thought that would make the oldest Fomorians possibly the first Dreamers who the Tuatha met. It really turns Changeling History on its head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T19:34:54-07:00","id":1320640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1320638#post1320638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But yes I imagine the Autumn Sidhe would be a big factor, but they would be a minority compared to a conquering Host.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was trying to imply that the commoners rally under the Autumn Sidhe's banner. In doing so, they gain the ability to rebel against the Arcadians, but it would be an Autumn who The Dreaming acknowledges as the victor in this situation.<br /> <br /> Actually, now that I think about it, you could tweak the lore so that only the Autumn Sidhe are in support of the Entitled Commoner idea. Elevating the other kiths to nobility as a reward for exemplary service in the war against the Arcadian Sidhe, while the Arcadians themselves would hotly deny the very idea of elevating commoners to such a station.<br /> <br /> At that point, it becomes a story about Meritocracy vs Monarchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T19:37:56-07:00","id":1320641,"title":"","content":"My idea though is the war never ended. Or it ended but the Player's group lost so they are on the lamb constantly from the ruling Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T06:45:16-07:00","id":1320732,"title":"","content":"Recognized as villains? Seems that the powerful presence of the Sidhe prevents widespread rejection of their rule. So many Sidhe powers and the powers that are available with the influx of glamour that comes with the Sidhe can re-write history. Cronus, Naming and Sovereign, along with the Sidhe birthrights make them nigh-impossible to soil their reputation to the masses (mortal, prodigal or fae).<br /> <br /> Those who oppose them will always be seen as conspiracy theorists by the majority. Of course playing a crew of characters that know &quot;the truth&quot; would make a fun game.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-25-2019, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T12:43:53-07:00","id":1320816,"title":"","content":"The Sidhe are a medieval dream. That's so much of the problem. Changelings are connected to freedom, creativity, passion, idealism, and wonder, at least in this game. Changeling: the Lost has it's points and virtues and beats the Vampire, werewolf, and Mage reboots by miles, but C:tD has its own profound delights. But the Sidhe are a major and limiting issue. In many ways they bring a 19th century conservative rejection of modernity into the game. The Sidhe are totally bound up in pre-Modern forms of power and hierarchy and stagnate the changeling society. In many ways they are Banality personified. <br /> <br /> In many ways they remind me of Fantasy Authors that are so impressed by Tolkien that they have to make every fantasy story a pseudo-Medieval pseudo-European, rehash. The right-wing politics showing up in millions of replays of the Jacobite Rebellions only the Bonnie Prince wins. Well Tolkien was a wonderful guy but is politics were trash, his vision of a technology free England was as unrealistic as it was reactionary. And Bonnie Prince Charlie was a drunken fascist and about the only monarch worse than the House of Hanover available to the Brits. The Sidhe are inherently unable to rule well, they will always be a force of Banality until they drop both the monarchy and the &quot;noble as rulers&quot; games.<br /> <br /> Heck, even the area book for the South had the Changelings in one part of the South inventing a new progressive form of government.<br /> <br /> For the Sidhe to be heroes, they need a viable ideal. Feudalism isn't it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 06-26-2019, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T19:03:29-07:00","id":1320873,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a> Sidhe don't merely embody the dream of feudal rule. They also embody the dreams of superior bloodlines, and the literally God given right to rule. They do not claim to be superior, they ARE superior. Or at least, the belief that they are superior is what spawned them into existence in the first place. They originate from a time in which rebelling against the government was a crime akin to heresy. The monarchies of the time carried the support of the church, and to speak out against the crown was effectively speaking out against the clergy as well.<br /> <br /> Why would the Sidhe (who were already perfect beings to begin with) feel the need, let alone the desire, to change themselves in order to make the commoners feel more comfortable? Peasants were not born to govern, and their opinions on the matter are irrelevant to one who's authority has been ordained by a higher power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T19:12:46-07:00","id":1320875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1320873#post1320873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Sidhe don't merely embody the dream of feudal rule. They also embody the dreams of superior bloodlines, and the literally God given right to rule. They do not claim to be superior, they ARE superior. Or at least, the belief that they are superior is what spawned them into existence in the first place. They originate from a time in which rebelling against the government was a crime akin to heresy. The monarchies of the time carried the support of the church, and to speak out against the crown was effectively speaking out against the clergy as well.<br /> <br /> Why would the Sidhe (who were already perfect beings to begin with) feel the need, let alone the desire, to change themselves in order to make the commoners feel more comfortable? Peasants were not born to govern, and their opinions on the matter are irrelevant to one who's authority has been ordained by a higher power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't say the Sidhe want to change. I say the Changelings either need to change the Sidhe or be rid of them. The Sidhe are an old and corrupt dream. If the Sidhe stay locked in 19th century reactionary politics and ideals they will either destroy the modern world or be destroyed by it. Both the Balor and Leathaun would love that. But few of the Sidhe outside of House Liam would care if the world died as long as their party went on. Typical of human nobles as well as the fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T19:24:07-07:00","id":1320876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1320875#post1320875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't say the Sidhe want to change. I say the Changelings either need to change the Sidhe or be rid of them. The Sidhe are an old and corrupt dream. If the Sidhe stay locked in 19th century reactionary politics and ideals they will either destroy the modern world or be destroyed by it. Both the Balor and Leathaun would love that. But few of the Sidhe outside of House Liam would care if the world died as long as their party went on. Typical of human nobles as well as the fae.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And looking at it from their point of view, they would be completely in the right of it. What species in the entire history of this planet has willfully chosen to let itself go extinct so that a different species can survive? The modern world is killing The Dreaming, the very source of life itself for all Fey. If mortals didn't embrace secular rationalism, the Changeling Way would never have been necessary, and the Fey would not be in the dire state they are in now. Purging the world of Autumn People and sparing true Dreamers may be the only way to prevent the Long Winter, and pull their kind back from the brink of annihilation.<br /> <br /> Those who stand with mortals know deep down that their efforts are for naught. The only thing they're doing is prolonging the inevitable decline. Unless they do something drastic, their kind is going to die out. And unlike the Sidhe, none of them seem to be coming up with tenable solutions to the problem.<br /> <br /> As it currently stands now, it's quite difficult to paint the Sidhe as being in the wrong, from a Fey's point of view. Sure, if you're a mortal, they sound like bad news. But mortals don't have to worry about the death of their entire species if they stop believing in old superstitions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-25-2019, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T21:05:56-07:00","id":1320886,"title":"","content":"Well actually it\u2019s more the rise of Monotheism and the taming of the Wilderness that causes the Changeling way to be Necessary, and the Plagues also helped with culminating Banality as a thing. In Dark Age Fae churches were their kryptonite a and often a source of banes. Only later did rationality further solidify the dying of Glamour and the rise of Banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T06:20:06-07:00","id":1320943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1320886#post1320886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well actually it\u2019s more the rise of Monotheism and the taming of the Wilderness that causes the Changeling way to be Necessary, and the Plagues also helped with culminating Banality as a thing. In Dark Age Fae churches were their kryptonite a and often a source of banes. Only later did rationality further solidify the dying of Glamour and the rise of Banality.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Dogma</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, the nastiest and most subversive aspect of the Weaver in my view of things. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> As far as the Sidhe and their role in Fae culture, I see it like this:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Tuatha's binding of the Fomorians coincided with the Weavers binding of the Wyrm, and started the problem. Binding the forces of Primordialism within the fabric of the Dreaming is a decidedly Weaver-ish undertaking, and has prevented the natural cycles of spirit and matter. Like a </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">tourniquet, though</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> meant to stop bleeding, if left on too long causes rot. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Sidhe live on the structures created by the Tuatha de Dannan. The dreams of nobility are a sort of placeholder to keep the ancient wards healthy (and the Dark asleep in their prisons), with the Houses meant to keep the bindings with tradition, heroism and grace (in Mage terms- Dynamic, Pattern and Questing Essence). But a great many Sidhe fled their duties, and left their lands unguarded and their people unprotected. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Now the Sidhe have returned to find that in their absence and neglect, the Dark has seeped into the world, and is poisoning the Dreaming. Horrible Nightmares once again have gained major footholds on the world through mans nastiest and greediest dreams, leaving Banality in its wake. They are panicking, trying to re-establish their holdings and make a stand. But they have forgotten much and are painfully anachronistic. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Few of the Sidhe remember much of this, with what they do remember being muddled up with stories and traditions. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-26-2019, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T07:12:23-07:00","id":1321712,"title":"","content":"When we were kids, were we so critical about fantasies of princesses and knights in shining armor?. When did we become so political about this stuff?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think this thread shows a very mature way of thinking that implies knowledge about causes and consequences, about the nuances of right and wrong, and a decent understanding of worldbuild...and Changeling isn't about that.<br /> <br /> Changeling it's about that time when we hadn't to consider if Disney classics were an apology to monarchy, Santa Claus a symbol of consumerism, etc.<br /> <br /> That time when we were &quot;impressed by Tolkien&quot; too, before we started to think in the implications of how the races are depicted. Being <i>impressed</i> in such an irrational way, w/o pondering if the morals presented there are <i>really</i> good to build a<i> real life </i>society...it's all that Glamour it's supposed to represent.<br /> <br /> Or at least that's my opinion.<br /> <br /> I'm glad that Shide exist and are the way they are...not that I would despise a game that presented them as the Bad Guys (it's easy enough), but I <i>get</i> why they weren't represented like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-01-2019, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T12:26:45-07:00","id":1321760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1321712#post1321712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When we were kids, were we so critical about fantasies of princesses and knights in shining armor?. When did we become so political about this stuff?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think this thread shows a very mature way of thinking that implies knowledge about causes and consequences, about the nuances of right and wrong, and a decent understanding of worldbuild...and Changeling isn't about that.<br /> <br /> Changeling it's about that time when we hadn't to consider if Disney classics were an apology to monarchy, Santa Claus a symbol of consumerism, etc.<br /> <br /> That time when we were &quot;impressed by Tolkien&quot; too, before we started to think in the implications of how the races are depicted. Being <i>impressed</i> in such an irrational way, w/o pondering if the morals presented there are <i>really</i> good to build a<i> real life </i>society...it's all that Glamour it's supposed to represent.<br /> <br /> Or at least that's my opinion.<br /> <br /> I'm glad that Shide exist and are the way they are...not that I would despise a game that presented them as the Bad Guys (it's easy enough), but I <i>get</i> why they weren't represented like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very well said, and I believe it provides further incentive to play a Childling character. Most people I've seen talking about the game on youtube seem to be opposed to the idea of playing one, for whatever reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T08:58:18-07:00","id":1322039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1321712#post1321712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When we were kids, were we so critical about fantasies of princesses and knights in shining armor?. When did we become so political about this stuff?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think this thread shows a very mature way of thinking that implies knowledge about causes and consequences, about the nuances of right and wrong, and a decent understanding of worldbuild...and Changeling isn't about that.<br /> <br /> Changeling it's about that time when we hadn't to consider if Disney classics were an apology to monarchy, Santa Claus a symbol of consumerism, etc.<br /> <br /> That time when we were &quot;impressed by Tolkien&quot; too, before we started to think in the implications of how the races are depicted. Being <i>impressed</i> in such an irrational way, w/o pondering if the morals presented there are <i>really</i> good to build a<i> real life </i>society...it's all that Glamour it's supposed to represent.<br /> <br /> Or at least that's my opinion.<br /> <br /> I'm glad that Shide exist and are the way they are...not that I would despise a game that presented them as the Bad Guys (it's easy enough), but I <i>get</i> why they weren't represented like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent points. However I would add that Changeling is also about the hurt of having dreams torn apart.<br /> <br /> When the Sidhe left, they betrayed that child-like devotion to land and king, like a parent who walks out or abuses those they should protect. A ravaging of their kingdoms so-to-speak. And now, the returned Sidhe are much like a deadbeat or violent parent who shows up looking to &quot;make things right&quot;, whether wanted or not.<br /> <br /> This of course is a sad, bitter and hurtful aspect of the game. Regaining or re-forging trust, love and honor in such a broken household is very very difficult. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But if done </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">courageously, could do much to repair the dreaming. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T04:59:06-07:00","id":1322200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1321760#post1321760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Very well said, and I believe it provides further incentive to play a Childling character. Most people I've seen talking about the game on youtube seem to be opposed to the idea of playing one, for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played Childlings. It was fun, as are Gumps and Wilders. But just because I can for fun go with the imaginative flow does not mean I must lose my rational mind. Tolkien, Dunsany, C. S. Lewis, and Yeats, are some of my favorite authors. I find many of their tales as rich in wisdom as in beauty. But all four were political idiots. I adore the wonder and beauty they brought but I don't follow blindly. My eyes are open, I can see both sides. I can see Charles Dickens' profound empathy and his racist jigoistic bigotry. I can still love the beauty of his tales, his worldview, and his personal character, while sidestepping the toxins. <br /> <br /> As Ursula Le Guin said &quot;A real adult is not a child who died, they are a child that lived!&quot; I never lost my child self. But I am an adult, a mere style and glamour can't excuse evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T05:45:35-07:00","id":1322203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322200#post1322200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've played Childlings. It was fun, as are Gumps and Wilders. But just because I can for fun go with the imaginative flow does not mean I must lose my rational mind. Tolkien, Dunsany, C. S. Lewis, and Yeats, are some of my favorite authors. I find many of their tales as rich in wisdom as in beauty. But all four were political idiots. I adore the wonder and beauty they brought but I don't follow blindly. My eyes are open, I can see both sides. I can see Charles Dickens' profound empathy and his racist jigoistic bigotry. I can still love the beauty of his tales, his worldview, and his personal character, while sidestepping the toxins.<br /> <br /> As Ursula Le Guin said &quot;A real adult is not a child who died, they are a child that lived!&quot; I never lost my child self. But I am an adult, a mere style and glamour can't excuse evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, when I was growing up, it was like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> said. I did not consider whether or not the characters, races, cultures and societies taking place in fictional worlds had anything to do with real life issues. The thought literally never even crossed my mind, because I personally did not even know those were supposed to be stereotypes. Much less had any knowledge of who those stereotypes were supposed to represent.<br /> <br /> It was not until later on in life, after years of people imposing their political ideologies and world views upon me, that my brain finally started to blend the world of fantasy and reality together. A change for which such people have earned my eternal scorn, as they practically killed my sense of child-like creativity, and the ability to enjoy a good fantasy setting, without subconsciously trying to associate it with real world situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T07:22:39-07:00","id":1322219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322200#post1322200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've played Childlings. It was fun, as are Gumps and Wilders. But just because I can for fun go with the imaginative flow does not mean I must lose my rational mind. Tolkien, Dunsany, C. S. Lewis, and Yeats, are some of my favorite authors. I find many of their tales as rich in wisdom as in beauty. But all four were political idiots. I adore the wonder and beauty they brought but I don't follow blindly. My eyes are open, I can see both sides. I can see Charles Dickens' profound empathy and his racist jigoistic bigotry. I can still love the beauty of his tales, his worldview, and his personal character, while sidestepping the toxins.<br /> <br /> As Ursula Le Guin said &quot;A real adult is not a child who died, they are a child that lived!&quot; I never lost my child self. But I am an adult, a mere style and glamour can't excuse evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't accusing YOU of not being Glamorous enough. I was merely talking about Changeling. You aren't a fictional character. And you are a human being and not a being made of dreams living in a fairytale society (aren't you?).<br /> <br /> That's why your glamour can't excuse evil.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1756_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1756\" data-vbnamecard=\"1756\">MythAdvocate</a> that there's much to be criticized, IOC, to the Shide. Just not so much because feudalism it's not an ideal political system.<br /> <br /> At least I can't see most Changelings (esp not Childlings) criticize THAT. Changelings are fae, fairytale morals are to be expected to some extent. Perhaps the human soul cares about politics that way, but I imagine the Fae soul cares more about the beauty of those tales than their political context (and atleast the 2nd edition book stated that much when explaining why the rebelion fails. It's not just that the Dreaming doesn't want, most Changelings don't want to change the system either).<br /> <br /> For Changelings Glamour CAN excuse evil. If that doesn't sound right...well, fae weren't so feared by humans for no reason. <hr /><br /> And now a word about Ficition:<br /> <br /> \u200bGod bless the fact that fiction doesn't need to respect moral <i>at every turn</i>. Because otherwise fantasy would be crippled...Imagine that. We would need to <b>forbidde </b>(or at least discourage the reading of) the books of Tolkien, Dunsany, C. S. Lewis, and Yeats on the grounds that they have evil messages. That you don't follow these messages matters not, spreading a toxic message it's nearly as inexcusable as enacting it.<br /> <br /> Same happens with most glamorous things. Conan the Barbarian, in my humble opinion, it's super glamorous and rightfully the Hero of his stories...but I wouldn't call him a role model (hopefully people understands not to imitate &quot;the best thing in life&quot;)<br /> <br /> It's bad that <i>good </i>characters in RPG often fight and kill?. <i><b>Well</b>,<b> some would say it IS</b></i>. Often RPG was criticized as &quot;promoting violence&quot; (and not only by Christians).<br /> <br /> My opinion it's that it isn't bad because RPG it's a fantasy and it's good for the mind to be able to release those dark impulses w/o being presured by real life morals and ethics. In my opinion, &quot;Evil people deserve to be killed&quot; it's aborrent, but I have no problem playing a Paladin<br /> <br /> Would you discourage little girls playing princesses because that promotes an unjust live of privilege that implies an oppressed class of 'peasants'?. Some would, comunists said that this was, in fact, necessary to change the world. But it's my opinion that as long as you understand the edge between fantasy and reality, you can have your scapisms. Does that make me <i>evil</i>?<br /> <br /> All in all, I like that Changeling is able to reproduce a fairytale society with some modern elements. I don't think that the Shide should be <i>represented </i>as evil just because they kinda <i>are. </i>Changeling does a good job of showcasing the problem of a vertical society, while at the same time justifying why the fae might enjoy to live in it more than in the &quot;real world&quot;.<br /> <br /> Changeling it's a game about the distance between fantasy and the real life. About the clash of fantasy and the &quot;real&quot; world. And about what is compromised (not necessarily lost) when growing up (hence why age difference it's so important). It's wrong to assume that Banality it's related evil. Banality it's also to go to your job rather than going to the quest to defeat a dragon because you care more to provide for your human family than for the fancy entertainments of the Freehold.<br /> <br /> It's entirely wrong to say that Glamour it's good and Banality evil. Or even that Glamour it's Dynamic and Banality Static. Banality it's what you need to shield yourslef against the worst of fantasy and interact with the real world, not having it is madness. Glamour it's what you need to interact with the world of myths and magic...which it's often quite Static. After all, many tales are, in a way, eternal and timeless. Like the &quot;chaoskampf&quot;. Like the Fae used to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-04-2019, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T16:23:25-07:00","id":1322299,"title":"","content":"You don\u2019t need to talk politics when saying Stealing someone\u2019s Body and banishing their soul to an Alien Realm is mighty wicked seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T04:07:09-07:00","id":1322382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322299#post1322299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don\u2019t need to talk politics when saying Stealing someone\u2019s Body and banishing their soul to an Alien Realm is mighty wicked seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. And the Sidhe claim that it is a gift to them doesn't excuse anything. If I force someone to take a multi-decade luxury vacation, keeping them away from their loved ones and home against their will, that's called kidnapping. It doesn't matter how nice the prison is, unlawful imprisonment is still a crime. The Sidhe should use the Changeling way or stay in Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T04:24:43-07:00","id":1322386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322299#post1322299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don\u2019t need to talk politics when saying Stealing someone\u2019s Body and banishing their soul to an Alien Realm is mighty wicked seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, from a human point of view. But we are talking about Fae here. These are the same beings that did not think twice to steal children from their cribs and replacing them with either their own or magical replicas. The same beings who could entertain a mortal quest for a night and when they returned them home decades, if not more, had actually passed. There is a reason people feared and respected the Fae, they are capricous and follow no mortal moral codes. To them what the Sidhe do is no more horrendous than stealing of children was, the mortal soul is sent to the Dreaming after all which is a fate most Fae would see as much more merciful than leaving them into the Banal world would have been so some might even see the Sidhe doing the mortals a favour. <br /> <br /> Some Sidhe, or any Fae actually, could argue that the Sidhe are sacrificimg themselves by inhabiting these mortal bodies with no True knowledge of what will happen to their own souls afterwards while they at the same time are giving these mortal souls home in the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s all a matter of perspective. None of this is particularly wicked thing from the Fae perspective while many things the Changelings do may be thought as wicked from the human point of view.<br /> <br /> The important thing here is to remember that the Commeners are still Fae even if they have been more in touch with mortals and they still have a Fae way of thinking and their morals are at best a mix between Fae and human and often much more tilted towards the Fae end of the spectrum.<br /> <br /> Wicked or not the Sidhe are true children of the Dreaming and their methods are just as much part of it as the commoners and their Changeling way. Is it truly more wicked to let mortal souls be their own entities that live on in the Dreaming while the Fae soul occupies the body meant for them than otit is to meld ones Fae soul with a mortal one taking over their whole soul instead of just replacing it and giving it it\u2019s own chance of existence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T04:34:56-07:00","id":1322388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322382#post1322382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. And the Sidhe claim that it is a gift to them doesn't excuse anything. If I force someone to take a multi-decade luxury vacation, keeping them away from their loved ones and home against their will, that's called kidnapping. It doesn't matter how nice the prison is, unlawful imprisonment is still a crime. The Sidhe should use the Changeling way or stay in Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how is Changeling way any more moral? If the Sidhe kidnap you to a forced luxury vacation the Changeling way invades your soul lettini a Fae soul to take over and control you, it forces you to suffer as the Changeling suffers much of it possibly in the hands of your previous loved ones who just cannot understand your Fae side. Is mind melting brain washing better than the luxury vacation? Is the forced union of two souls into one somehow better than to allow both to exist at the same time?<br /> <br /> All Fae can be pointed equally wicked if one wishes to do so. Of course the Sidhe see their way as better and more merciful it is them doing it after all. Same can be said of commoners who see the Changeling Way as more merciful because it is the road they chose. Much of the books are written from the perspective of those who basically posssess human souls and who claim those Fae who possess human bodies are the wicked ones and so that is the perspective we mostly get saturated with and which therefor sounds more moral to us.<br /> <br /> But that is perhaps the best way to put it. Sidhe possess bodies of mortals while the commoners possess the souls of mortals. Which is more wicked? Or are they both equally wicked from the mortal perspective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T12:48:30-07:00","id":1322478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322382#post1322382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. And the Sidhe claim that it is a gift to them doesn't excuse anything. If I force someone to take a multi-decade luxury vacation, keeping them away from their loved ones and home against their will, that's called kidnapping. It doesn't matter how nice the prison is, unlawful imprisonment is still a crime. The Sidhe should use the Changeling way or stay in Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sending mortals souls to the homeland of the Fae is a precious gift...<br /> <br /> I'm sure the Celts would <a href=\"https://youtu.be/uqOqEU1xwxI\" target=\"_blank\">hotly dispute</a> that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Given how the Sidhe tend to look down upon mortals as it is, even to the point that they were planning to exterminate all the non-Dreamers at one point, I'm going to assume the ones trapped in Arcadia are running for their lives. If they weren't killed by fire breathing Dragons, poisonous Manticores, and child snatching Hags within the first few hours of arrival.<br /> <br /> And as for that multi decade long vacation... Yeah, what happens to the mortal after the Sidhe is done with them? Because as far as I know, the only way they leave the host is after they've DIED!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-05-2019, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T13:30:38-07:00","id":1322485,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s not possessing the soul the Changeling way fuses you with a soul. Or do you consider Avatars Parasites too? Or is your brain a parasite taking advantage of your body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T13:54:03-07:00","id":1322492,"title":"","content":"Who ARE the bad guys in Changeling?<br /> Beyond Banality, that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T14:08:35-07:00","id":1322494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322478#post1322478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sending mortals souls to the homeland of the Fae is a precious gift...<br /> <br /> I'm sure the Celts would <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/uqOqEU1xwxI&quot;]hotly</a> dispute[/URL] that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Given how the Sidhe tend to look down upon mortals as it is, even to the point that they were planning to exterminate all the non-Dreamers at one point, I'm going to assume the ones trapped in Arcadia are running for their lives. If they weren't killed by fire breathing Dragons, poisonous Manticores, and child snatching Hags within the first few hours of arrival.<br /> <br /> And as for that multi decade long vacation... Yeah, what happens to the mortal after the Sidhe is done with them? Because as far as I know, the only way they leave the host is after they've DIED!</div> </div> </div> </div>Please note the sarcasm, it was spread thick. The Sidhe claim that sending mortals to Arcadia is a high honnor and gift. I was pointing out the flaws in their stories.<br /> <br /> With the Changeling way your born in that body and the fay soul is the soul period. No kidnapping or torture.<br /> <br /> I think about the twin Sidhe in the Ireland sourcebook who, in order to be born twins, swaped out two fetuses! Who would have promptly died in Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-05-2019, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T14:45:33-07:00","id":1322505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322494#post1322494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please note the sarcasm, it was spread thick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I was just poking fun at the idea, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322485#post1322485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not possessing the soul the Changeling way fuses you with a soul. Or do you consider Avatars Parasites too? Or is your brain a parasite taking advantage of your body?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I learned in school that there are different types of parasites. At least one of which (symbiotic) is actually beneficial to the host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T14:50:25-07:00","id":1322506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322492#post1322492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who ARE the bad guys in Changeling?<br /> Beyond Banality, that is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought it was the Thallain, who are born from dreams of a more savage time, before the Tuatha showed mortals how to act like civilized beings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T14:50:45-07:00","id":1322507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322485#post1322485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not possessing the soul the Changeling way fuses you with a soul. Or do you consider Avatars Parasites too? Or is your brain a parasite taking advantage of your body?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well every human is born with a brain not every human is born with an alien entitys soul fused to their own. You see such fusion as a good thing, so do most commoners, but can we really say that? It still changes the soul and fate of that particular human making it into something else, the human soul gets to make desicions only when Banality overwhelms the Fae or if the Fae side is forced down by Chimerical death.<br /> <br /> Sidhe do replace the soul saving it from such fusion, we do not know what happens to those souls in Arcadia for all we know they either live on there in splendour or perhaps in suffering or they may over the years become more Fae than human becoming new Fae souls. The truth of the matter is we know nothing really of their fates.<br /> <br /> So can we really condamn the Sidhe without knowing the fate of the souls they take? In my opinion we cannot. Those souls may get it better than any on Autumn lands or they may have it worse, but DA: Fae does heavily imply that they become Changelings, similarly to how the Fae left to replace them do. If DA: Fae then is taken as proof the Sidhe way of doing things creates two Changelings for the price of one, the Sidhe and the Changeling that is grown from the human soul in the Dreaming while the Changeling way fuses two souls together to create one composite being.<br /> <br /> Again try to remember these are Fae we are talking about human morality is not really their thing so we shouldn\u2019t try to judge them according to human mores. To see the Fae side of things think if either method breakes the escheat or the Courts laws if not it is not really immoral to the Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T15:01:55-07:00","id":1322509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322505#post1322505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know, I was just poking fun at the idea, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I learned in school that there are different types of parasites. At least one of which (symbiotic) is actually beneficial to the host.</div> </div> </div> </div>Symbiotes are not parasites they are symbiotes by definition. And the Changing way alters the nature of the soul. You are as much Fae as you are human.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T15:13:37-07:00","id":1322512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322507#post1322507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So can we really condamn the Sidhe without knowing the fate of the souls they take? In my opinion we cannot. Those souls may get it better than any on Autumn lands or they may have it worse, but DA: Fae does heavily imply that they become Changelings, similarly to how the Fae left to replace them do. If DA: Fae then is taken as proof the Sidhe way of doing things creates two Changelings for the price of one, the Sidhe and the Changeling that is grown from the human soul in the Dreaming while the Changeling way fuses two souls together to create one composite being.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they do become Fae themselves, then I would agree that seems to be more of a blessing than a curse. But if they remain human, then being sent to Arcadia would be a living nightmare. First of all, anybody who's familiar with traditional folk lore knows that the <b>Fae are ass holes</b>, and there is a very good reason why parents used Fairy Tales to scare their children into behaving properly.<br /> <br /> Second of all, we can assume from the way the Sidhe conduct themselves that Arcadian society is still very much trapped in the 1500's. Possibly even more primitive than that, depending on how far back they stagnated. Any human from the modern world who gets thrown into it is going to be in for the world's biggest culture shock, as they struggle to cope with laws and regulations that haven't been in effect for hundreds of years.<br /> <br /> So to reiterate, being sent to Arcadia might be tolerable, if you transform into a Fae yourself. But if you remain a human, you would be scrambling for the nearest exit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T16:49:45-07:00","id":1322524,"title":"","content":"Its not a blessing if you get your life taken from you without your consent and someone else steals your wife or husband and family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T16:51:43-07:00","id":1322525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322512#post1322512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Fae are ass holes</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. This is my point. It applies to both Commoners and the Sidhe. Hence neither will actually see how the Sidhe possess humans as evil or immoral nor do they see any problems in forcing soul fusion to mortals. It is only mentioned that it is critisized by some for the potential destruction of the human soul <b>unnecessarily</b>. Note the bolded part. It is not the destruction of the soul the Changelings are against but that they see it as unnecessary due to Changeling Way.<br /> <br /> Like said the Fae concept of moral is different from ours. The Escheat\u2019s Right of Life explicitly mentions it applying to Fae lives, it does nothing to protect mortals. Same is True of the rest of the laws even Right of Dream only forbids messing with human creative process and has nothing to do with actually protecting humans, same with Right of Ignorance which is meant to keep mortals unaware of the Fae. Neither Court has any real probihition against harming mortals either. You keep looking this far too much from the mortal perspective and too little from the Fae one. Remember Fae are assholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T16:56:48-07:00","id":1322527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322524#post1322524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not a blessing if you get your life taken from you without your consent and someone else steals your wife or husband and family.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Meh, you (allegedly) gain immortality, magical powers, and the freedom to experience the joys of life for the first time over and over again. Sounds like a pretty sweet bargain... assuming that's how it actually works out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T17:00:32-07:00","id":1322528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322527#post1322527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Meh, you (allegedly) gain immortality, magical powers, and the freedom to experience the joys of life for the first time over and over again. Sounds like a pretty sweet bargain... assuming that's how it actually works out.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some, but a lot of people don't want to have some selfish Faery Prince bang their wife and not give a crap about their kids, meanwhile a number of fates could await you, what if you become something akin to a Redcap and in the real world you were Jason Mamoa?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T03:05:58-07:00","id":1322917,"title":"","content":"I always play sidhe, but it seems like other people always want the sidhe to be badguys. It\u2019s like all WoD players want to \u201cfight the power\u201d, but they don\u2019t understand that, despite being leaders of the changelings, the sidhe are not the power. (Mortals are) Before I get too far into that diatribe, I will say that there is plenty of room for sidhe to be villains of any chronicle.. in many ways, the sidhe represent the best and worst of changelings, but why should any changeling be relegated to being \u201cthe badguys\u201d when all changelings have the potential to be both great heroes and great villains. I mean, there are plenty of stories of evil and overbearing lords, but wouldn\u2019t a story of an evil craftsman (boggin) be as interesting and probably more unique? Isn\u2019t it a little disrespectful of the other kith to say that only the sidhe can be \u201cbadguys\u201d among the changelings? <br /> <br /> I also want to push back a little on the idea of the sidhe being the embodiment of feudal fantasy.. the sidhe are the embodiment of romantic fantasy. The seelie sidhe actually don\u2019t have a big problem with ideas like constitutional monarchies and republics and the like.. High king David created the parliament of dreams, which is the actual governing body of Concordia, and sidhe in Concordia are generally respected more for their title rather than their land. Meanwhile, oaths are important to all changelings, not just the sidhe.. so feudalism, government based on land ownership and oaths, isn\u2019t part of being sidhe any more than it\u2019s part of being any other changeling. On the other hand, epics, quests, romances, great betrayals and acts self-sacrifice and heroism.. that\u2019s what makes a sidhe.. they are all about romantic idealism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T03:37:09-07:00","id":1322921,"title":"","content":"Nobody says anything about only the Sidhe can be badguys. That is a bit strawmany.<br /> <br /> Yes yes we all know Mortals outnumber everyone, yawn.<br /> <br /> <br /> But my basic assumption for this scenario is the Sidhe are even more sinister and overtly the Antagonist then the normal setting, they would also probably have different crunch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T11:31:59-07:00","id":1323002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322921#post1322921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody says anything about only the Sidhe can be badguys. That is a bit strawmany.<br /> <br /> Yes yes we all know Mortals outnumber everyone, yawn.<br /> <br /> <br /> But my basic assumption for this scenario is the Sidhe are even more sinister and overtly the Antagonist then the normal setting, they would also probably have different crunch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhmm.. you\u2019ve suggested that the sidhe should be turned into complete villains while also saying that other changelings.. I\u2019ll let others decide whether my comment was \u201cstrawmany\u201d. I\u2019m also not suggesting that mortals are \u201cthe power\u201d because they are numerous.. I\u2019m suggesting that mortals are \u201cthe power\u201d because changelings need mortals in order to survive.. a single mortal who is easily inspired can be very good for changelings, while a single mortal who refuses to dream can be very dangerous to an entire freehold of changelings. To vampires, individual mortals might be food supply, to werewolves they are flunkies, to mages a single mortal is an inconvenience, to a changeling a single mortal could mean life or death.<br /> <br /> But for the sake of furthering the discussion, the current changeling paradigm already supports sidhe as being great villains. The Ailil hang out with Nephandi, Sabbat, and BSD\u2019s.. do you think they somehow aren\u2019t evil? The Baylor hang with Formorii and like to permakill fae, and the Leanhaun abuse mortals and partake in psychic vampirism. If you want to make the sidhe \u201cmore villainous\u201d, just have the Unseelie and/ or Winter Court take all the most influential positions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T13:38:30-07:00","id":1323043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1322917#post1322917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn\u2019t it a little disrespectful of the other kith to say that only the sidhe can be \u201cbadguys\u201d among the changelings?<br /> <br /> I also want to push back a little on the idea of the sidhe being the embodiment of feudal fantasy.. the sidhe are the embodiment of romantic fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1 - Of course it is, because it sounds like the players have forgotten that REDCAPS are a thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2 - Actually, feudal fantasy is exactly it. Remember, the Sidhe were actually present during the time of feudal dynasties, and they abandoned the Autumn World while they were still in place. I highly doubt that anybody who lived back in that day and age saw their existence as anything one might describe as romantic. Remember, that was an age in which the concept of marriage was more of a political maneuver, rather than having anything to do with actual relationships. Combine that with plagues, widespread poverty, lack of proper medical knowledge, and a whole slew of other problems that would dramatically shorten your life expectancy.<br /> <br /> The Sidhe who did adapt to the modern world became the Autumn Sidhe, and their Arcadian counterparts view them as corrupted, and an insult to everything the Sidhe stand for. The Arcadians only took human hosts because the only other choice available to them was death. And many Sidhe (like those of House Aesin) hate the very idea of Entitled Commoners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-08-2019, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T14:06:45-07:00","id":1323047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323002#post1323002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want to make the sidhe \u201cmore villainous\u201d, just have the Unseelie and/ or Winter Court take all the most influential positions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does everybody think the Unseelie Court are the defacto villains? You know what the Unseelie stand for? Breaking from tradition and embracing freedom. That sounds like the exact kind of court somebody who's trying to oppose tyrannical Sidhe (with their old world views) would be eager to join up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T14:41:12-07:00","id":1323058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323047#post1323047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why does everybody think the Unseelie Court are the defacto villains? You know what the Unseelie stand for? Breaking from tradition and embracing freedom. That sounds like the exact kind of court somebody who's trying to oppose tyrannical Sidhe (with their old world views) would be eager to join up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Damn right! I think the corrupting influence of stasis is the cause of all that is rotten. Cycles are what the fae are all about. Without winter, there is no spring. Doesn't mean its bad. The good guy/bad guy paradigm is ridiculous in storytelling anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-08-2019, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T18:12:00-07:00","id":1323091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323047#post1323047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why does everybody think the Unseelie Court are the defacto villains? You know what the Unseelie stand for? Breaking from tradition and embracing freedom. That sounds like the exact kind of court somebody who's trying to oppose tyrannical Sidhe (with their old world views) would be eager to join up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> My issue is that most people don\u2019t even seem to remember that the unseelie court and the Winter Court even exist, let alone do they view them as \u201cdefacto villains\u201d. To be clear, I don\u2019t know enough about th actual unseelie court to really call them villains.. I definitely call the Winter Court villains though and they kinda seem to hide behind the unseelie court. As far as I know, the actual unseelie court is just part of the cycle, while the Winter Court seeks to end the cycle. The Winter court \u201cbreaks from tradition and embraces freedom\u201d in much the same way as serial killers and mass murderers do.<br /> <br /> The villain/hero paradigm may be ridiculous, but the struggle to maintain ridiculous paradigms is what changeling is all about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T18:49:40-07:00","id":1323100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323091#post1323091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My issue is that most people don\u2019t even seem to remember that the unseelie court and the Winter Court even exist, let alone do they view them as \u201cdefacto villains\u201d. To be clear, I don\u2019t know enough about th actual unseelie court to really call them villains.. I definitely call the Winter Court villains though and they kinda seem to hide behind the unseelie court. As far as I know, the actual unseelie court is just part of the cycle, while the Winter Court seeks to end the cycle. The Winter court \u201cbreaks from tradition and embraces freedom\u201d in much the same way as serial killers and mass murderers do.<br /> <br /> The villain/hero paradigm may be ridiculous, but the struggle to maintain ridiculous paradigms is what changeling is all about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, one of the reasons for the Unseelie Court's bad reputation is the fact that they have practically &quot;abandoned the Dreaming.&quot; Their reasoning for doing so is that they feel the Dreaming abandoned them first, so they are not under any obligation to continue serving it. They also abide by the outlook that as long as there are humans in the world, there will always be Dreamers, and so they are far more careless about the usage of Glamour than the Seelie Court are. Their more traditionalist counterparts prefer to hoard Glamour, and only use it when they feel there is a legitimate need for it.<br /> <br /> Another reason for why they might be seen as villains stems from their connection to the Shadow Court, which is a secret faction operating from within the Unseelie Court. <br /> <br /> Although the Shadow Court wishes to restore the tradition of ruling by cycles, it contains a large number of House Balor and Thallain among its ranks. Since these Kiths are typically viewed as monsters and servants of the Fomorians, it's understandable why players would jump to the conclusion that they must have malicious intentions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T19:06:32-07:00","id":1323104,"title":"","content":"Setting as written there really is no way for Royalists (be they Sidhe or Loyalist Commoners) to be anything but villains - you don\u2019t ABANDON YOUR SUBJECTS, then come back expecting to still have a right to rule.<br /> <br /> If they\u2019re meant to be anything other than the worst, the history needs an overhaul so that the Sidhe have a more Arthurian tragic-noble fall, or sacrificed themselves so the Changeling Way Ritual would be possible, etc - something that makes belief in their leadership a remotely rational moral position, instead of making those who fled to Arcadia and left their subjects behind the most craven of worthless cowards, as is currently the inevitable conclusion of the canon history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T19:12:21-07:00","id":1323105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323091#post1323091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My issue is that most people don\u2019t even seem to remember that the unseelie court and the Winter Court even exist, let alone do they view them as \u201cdefacto villains\u201d. To be clear, I don\u2019t know enough about th actual unseelie court to really call them villains.. I definitely call the Winter Court villains though and they kinda seem to hide behind the unseelie court. As far as I know, the actual unseelie court is just part of the cycle, while the Winter Court seeks to end the cycle. The Winter court \u201cbreaks from tradition and embraces freedom\u201d in much the same way as serial killers and mass murderers do.<br /> <br /> The villain/hero paradigm may be ridiculous, but the struggle to maintain ridiculous paradigms is what changeling is all about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is a potential project. Seasonal courts as of spiritual houses. Something more in line with nature, the moon and such. Perhaps allowing for Spirit Links ala Nunehi and Garou. <br /> <br /> Perhaps seasonal houses would make an alternative for the Autumn Sidhe and Commoner leaders during the interregnum. Kind of like totems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-08-2019, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T23:23:54-07:00","id":1323133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323105#post1323105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here is a potential project. Seasonal courts as of spiritual houses. Something more in line with nature, the moon and such. Perhaps allowing for Spirit Links ala Nunehi and Garou.<br /> <br /> Perhaps seasonal houses would make an alternative for the Autumn Sidhe and Commoner leaders during the interregnum. Kind of like totems.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a cool idea, Seasonal Houses instead of Seasonal Courts!<br /> <br /> I do feel that after the Nobles left, there totally would be Commoners who want to raise up new nobility. So the game doesn't change completely you don't need a lot of them but I feel like there would be at least some new nobles rising up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But I got the basic idea for this thread from that Walk through the Dreaming Podcast, where they said they believe early Drafts of the game had the Sidhe take up a more prominently antagonistic role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T03:33:25-07:00","id":1323161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323104#post1323104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting as written there really is no way for Royalists (be they Sidhe or Loyalist Commoners) to be anything but villains - you don\u2019t ABANDON YOUR SUBJECTS, then come back expecting to still have a right to rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that should be the truth of any respectable leaders, there are countless instances of mortals citing their claim to a particular territory just because their ancestors lived there hundreds of years ago. Once again, it's important to remember not just who the Fey are, but what they are as well. The Fey did not start out as humans, they started out as living dreams, sentient concepts, and physical aspirations that mortals believed in at the time. They did not interpret the world in the same way mortals do, because that is not the mentality which gave them life.<br /> <br /> The Changeling Way allowed them to develop such perspective, however. Becoming half human expanded their horizons and gave them a shield against the Banality which threatened to destroy them. Unfortunately for Changeling society, the majority of Sidhe refused to partake in this ritual, and just snatched the bodies of the closest mortal they could get their hands on. Arcadian Sidhe are the closest thing to a &quot;true&quot; Fey that the Kithain have to offer, because they remain uncorrupted by the influence of mortal society. Autumn Sidhe did allow themselves to merge with human souls, and the idea of such a transformation is appalling to their Arcadian cousins.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the grand scheme of things, you're right. The mortals of the Autumn World no longer believe in the same ideals which gave birth to Arcadia in the first place, and the Arcadian Sidhe who still adhere to them are pushing a very large boulder up a very steep hill. But so long as they continue to cling to the purity of their Fairy souls, they are fundamentally incapable of realizing that fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T13:49:45-07:00","id":1323271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323104#post1323104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting as written there really is no way for Royalists (be they Sidhe or Loyalist Commoners) to be anything but villains - you don\u2019t ABANDON YOUR SUBJECTS, then come back expecting to still have a right to rule.<br /> <br /> If they\u2019re meant to be anything other than the worst, the history needs an overhaul so that the Sidhe have a more Arthurian tragic-noble fall, or sacrificed themselves so the Changeling Way Ritual would be possible, etc - something that makes belief in their leadership a remotely rational moral position, instead of making those who fled to Arcadia and left their subjects behind the most craven of worthless cowards, as is currently the inevitable conclusion of the canon history.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The high king activated an oath and called them all back to Arcadia \u201cto solve the problem of the sundering and upcoming shattering\u201d. The Gwydion simply couldn\u2019t ignore their oath. The Dougal knew that they would be instrumental in solving the problem. Only house Fiona could resist, because lady Fiona was in love with a mortal which activates her house\u2019s boon. Houses Eiluned, Liam and Fiona all tried to make sure their domains would be in good hands while they were gone.. as they were forced away against their will and they did everything they could to get back. As soon as possible, I don\u2019t really see how you could view these houses as villains.<br /> <br /> Some parents need to leave their kids sometimes, so they hire a babysitter. Does that mean the babysitter has the right to keep the kid when the parent comes back? Is the parent \u201cevil\u201d because they left their kid and expected to get the kid back when they came home?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T15:15:03-07:00","id":1323291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323271#post1323271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The high king activated an oath and called them all back to Arcadia \u201cto solve the problem of the sundering and upcoming shattering\u201d. The Gwydion simply couldn\u2019t ignore their oath. The Dougal knew that they would be instrumental in solving the problem. Only house Fiona could resist, because lady Fiona was in love with a mortal which activates her house\u2019s boon. Houses Eiluned, Liam and Fiona all tried to make sure their domains would be in good hands while they were gone.. as they were forced away against their will and they did everything they could to get back. As soon as possible, I don\u2019t really see how you could view these houses as villains.<br /> <br /> Some parents need to leave their kids sometimes, so they hire a babysitter. Does that mean the babysitter has the right to keep the kid when the parent comes back? Is the parent \u201cevil\u201d because they left their kid and expected to get the kid back when they came home?</div> </div> </div> </div>We aren\u2019t talking about baby sitter keeping the kids, we\u2019re talking about abandoned kids who grew up to follow that analogy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T16:09:08-07:00","id":1323303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323271#post1323271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some parents need to leave their kids sometimes, so they hire a babysitter. Does that mean the babysitter has the right to keep the kid when the parent comes back? Is the parent \u201cevil\u201d because they left their kid and expected to get the kid back when they came home?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Parents who hire baby sitters are gone for maybe a couple hours at most.<br /> <br /> Parents who walk out on their kids for decades, only to show up unannounced and act like everything can go back to normal is a completely different story.<br /> <br /> My ancestors were Arch Dukes of France. Does that mean I have the right to fly there, demand they hand over the crown jewels, and declare me the rightful leader of their country?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T20:23:28-07:00","id":1323353,"title":"","content":"Also do people feel the Sidhe are intended to rule lands and Fae that are outside the Kithain? The Nunnehi for instance don't have the Noble commoner divide and Turtle Island was their Territory, and the Sidhe even allied with them rather than ruled them. And the Merfolk are Nobles themselves, and the Menehune have their own Nobles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T00:37:36-07:00","id":1323390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323291#post1323291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We aren\u2019t talking about baby sitter keeping the kids, we\u2019re talking about abandoned kids who grew up to follow that analogy.</div> </div> </div> </div> In the analogy, the commoners are the babysitters, not the kids. As we know, fae are immortal beings who perceive time differently from mortals. We also know that the sidhe, during the resurgence, had no memory of the time that had passed in Arcadia, so as far as they knew, they had left one day to solve a problem for the sake of all fae, and they came back the next day to find some commoners were claiming their domains and titles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T03:52:58-07:00","id":1323410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323390#post1323390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the analogy, the commoners are the babysitters, not the kids. As we know, fae are immortal beings who perceive time differently from mortals. We also know that the sidhe, during the resurgence, had no memory of the time that had passed in Arcadia, so as far as they knew, they had left one day to solve a problem for the sake of all fae, and they came back the next day to find some commoners were claiming their domains and titles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean we get the jist that they basically were terrified of Reincarnating and instead chose to continue their current incarnation... but the consequences of that is they will be in theory gone after this life.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <br /> Also what about when we start running out of Arcadian Sidhe? Maybe that should be another thread... but its bound to eventually happen, unless there are mysteries at play keeping them streaming in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","user":"Eldagusto","date":".  more 07-10-2019, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T10:54:05-07:00","id":1323471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323410#post1323410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also what about when we start running out of Arcadian Sidhe? Maybe that should be another thread... but its bound to eventually happen, unless there are mysteries at play keeping them streaming in.</div> </div> </div> </div>They might be reincarnated anyway, and just not remember. The Dreaming is endless right? And that means that there could be a numberless host of fae spirits dwelling in alternate timelines, fantasy worlds and other realms of legend. So why would they run out?<br /> <br /> For my own games, I deal with this as either the Sidhe become Autumn Sidhe over time, become shadow fae (a type of Legendary Plasmic) upon their death or take part in dark rituals that re-bind their fae soul to a mortal child.<br /> <br /> Similarly, in my home games fae of all kiths killed by Cold Iron become plasmic entities in the Shadowlands, where they maintain some potent holdings. As plasmics they appear as the more pale and deathly fae of legends and may have some connection to Thallain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-10-2019, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T19:12:34-07:00","id":1323578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323471#post1323471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They might be reincarnated anyway, and just not remember. The Dreaming is endless right? And that means that there could be a numberless host of fae spirits dwelling in alternate timelines, fantasy worlds and other realms of legend. So why would they run out?<br /> <br /> For my own games, I deal with this as either the Sidhe become Autumn Sidhe over time, become shadow fae (a type of Legendary Plasmic) upon their death or take part in dark rituals that re-bind their fae soul to a mortal child.<br /> <br /> Similarly, in my home games fae of all kiths killed by Cold Iron become plasmic entities in the Shadowlands, where they maintain some potent holdings. As plasmics they appear as the more pale and deathly fae of legends and may have some connection to Thallain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> See I think it dilutes the danger and consequences of actions if the Sidhe just reincarnate like normal without becoming Autumn Sidhe first. I had two basic Ideas, the Sidhe either become Clarichaun (and other commoners upon death) or they become Fae Ghosts. Though them becoming ghosts after being killed with Cold Iron seems a problem because Cold Iron Obliterates their soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T05:31:22-07:00","id":1323650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323578#post1323578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See I think it dilutes the danger and consequences of actions if the Sidhe just reincarnate like normal without becoming Autumn Sidhe first. I had two basic Ideas, the Sidhe either become Clarichaun (and other commoners upon death) or they become Fae Ghosts. Though them becoming ghosts after being killed with Cold Iron seems a problem because Cold Iron Obliterates their soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legendary Plasmics are anomalous. They are not Wraiths, but something else entirely. There are many legends of faerie like beings whom Iron is not an issue, though these are monstrous and very alien beings. Banshees are an obvious addition to this, but the Cailleach (death hag), Jarnvidjur (troll hags), Sirens, Tenebrae (Greek/Roman death spirits) and assorted Psychopomps all fit the bill for creatures of both Death and Glamour. Some of these creatures might also be Kinain or Faerie animals. <br /> <br /> Of course, these creatures could &quot;just&quot; be Umbrood. Personally, I would treat such beings as Chimera with a &quot;Nightmare Shield&quot; that can be used to resist Banality and to soak Iron, and to cause Bedlam in Changelings. I would also say that such creatures could suck Glamour from the Pathos of Wraiths and Willpower from vamps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-11-2019, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T11:16:34-07:00","id":1324009,"title":"","content":"I like to think that dead Arcadians are recruited by House Danaan, who pretty much spend all their time within the Dreaming and only interact with the Autumn World when they feel it's necessary.<br /> <br /> As for those killed by Cold Iron, I also like the idea that House Beaumayn actually turn out to be right, and that death by such instruments purifies the soul of Banality, restoring them to how they were before they subjected themselves to the Changeling Way. The drawback is that they can not linger in the Autumn World anymore, and so they must retreat to the Deep Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is probably just be me wishing for a happy ending to what I feel is the most depressing game in the WoD franchise... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T19:19:06-07:00","id":1324331,"title":"","content":"Canonically, fae who die by cold iron become wraiths. Meaning the sluagh know about the Martyrs of Beltaine, since they were contacted by their furious wraiths after the Night of Iron Knives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T13:27:09-07:00","id":1325053,"title":"","content":"Part of the Arcadian sidhe's problem is that they remained static while in Arcadia. Autumn sidhe haven't, partly because of how they were raised, partly from being merged with a human soul rather than kicking it out of body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T22:13:32-07:00","id":1325874,"title":"","content":"I just figured out what happens to the human souls the sidhe send to Arcadia.There's mention of Arcadian humans. And the books say that humans in the Dreaming or in Arcadia who have no Banality can't leave. Comatose humans also can't leave, they just hang around and watch things, like an especially vivid dream. So when a sidhe is Undone, the human soul taken to Arcadia or otherwise lost in the Dreaming, like Harroth's, get a sudden influx of Banality when the Arcadian sidhe dies. That lasts long enough for the otherwise stranded mortal soul to find their way home again, taking back their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","user":"Saint Michael","date":". 07-19-2019, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T10:44:15-07:00","id":1326034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323104#post1323104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they\u2019re meant to be anything other than the worst, the history needs an overhaul so that the Sidhe have a more Arthurian tragic-noble fall, or sacrificed themselves so the Changeling Way Ritual would be possible, etc - something that makes belief in their leadership a remotely rational moral position, instead of making those who fled to Arcadia and left their subjects behind the most craven of worthless cowards, as is currently the inevitable conclusion of the canon history.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sadly not experienced with Authurian myth beyond the Sword in the Stone, but if I have my facts right, Arthur lost his kingdom because <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-JJ-RSyhLpo\" target=\"_blank\">Guenivier cheated on him with Lancelot.</a> And while Arthur was busy chasing the fugitives across the countryside (since the punishment for adultery in those days was death), Morgan le Fey invaded the kingdom and successfully managed to conquer it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-19-2019, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T02:54:46-08:00","id":1364308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323650#post1323650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Legendary Plasmics are anomalous. They are not Wraiths, but something else entirely. There are many legends of faerie like beings whom Iron is not an issue, though these are monstrous and very alien beings. Banshees are an obvious addition to this, but the Cailleach (death hag), Jarnvidjur (troll hags), Sirens, Tenebrae (Greek/Roman death spirits) and assorted Psychopomps all fit the bill for creatures of both Death and Glamour. Some of these creatures might also be Kinain or Faerie animals. <br /> <br /> Of course, these creatures could &quot;just&quot; be Umbrood. Personally, I would treat such beings as Chimera with a &quot;Nightmare Shield&quot; that can be used to resist Banality and to soak Iron, and to cause Bedlam in Changelings. I would also say that such creatures could suck Glamour from the Pathos of Wraiths and Willpower from vamps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their are Banshee from the shining host that are Sidhe Wraiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 01-31-2020, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T17:14:53-08:00","id":1365401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1320371-what-if-the-setting-recognized-the-sidhe-as-the-badguys?p=1323002#post1323002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uhmm.. you\u2019ve suggested that the sidhe should be turned into complete villains while also saying that other changelings.. I\u2019ll let others decide whether my comment was \u201cstrawmany\u201d. I\u2019m also not suggesting that mortals are \u201cthe power\u201d because they are numerous.. I\u2019m suggesting that mortals are \u201cthe power\u201d because changelings need mortals in order to survive.. a single mortal who is easily inspired can be very good for changelings, while a single mortal who refuses to dream can be very dangerous to an entire freehold of changelings. To vampires, individual mortals might be food supply, to werewolves they are flunkies, to mages a single mortal is an inconvenience, to a changeling a single mortal could mean life or death.<br /> <br /> But for the sake of furthering the discussion, the current changeling paradigm already supports sidhe as being great villains. The Ailil hang out with Nephandi, Sabbat, and BSD\u2019s.. do you think they somehow aren\u2019t evil? The Baylor hang with Formorii and like to permakill fae, and the Leanhaun abuse mortals and partake in psychic vampirism. If you want to make the sidhe \u201cmore villainous\u201d, just have the Unseelie and/ or Winter Court take all the most influential positions.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I never heard of the Dragons hanging out with such vile company,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T11:03:24-07:00","id":1376730,"title":"","content":"Are the earlier editions of Changeling: The Dreaming less obvious with their subtext? Cause I've read 20th Anniversary Edition, and that thing releases a miasma of the stuff, whenever I open the PDF.<br /> <br /> The Sidhe are quite obviously a stand-in for &quot;The Man&quot; (the Arcadian Sidhe literally took over the bodies of the 1%, when they returned to the Autumn World). And just like &quot;The Man&quot; in real life, they aren't recognized as &quot;the badguys&quot; for their heinous acts or hoarding of freeholds or refusal to help the common changeling in time of great strife, except by the fringes of society (i.e. those weirdos that went about pointing out the obvious subtext in fantasy novels, ruining your ability to read those kinds of books without being hyper aware of what the author was so clearly trying to say).<br /> <br /> And, like, that's exactly as it should be. That's how everything in The World of Darkness is (unless you and your Story Teller decide to just ignore all that stuff, and just have a fun little story about some fantasy creatures in the real world trying real hard to not die horrifically). It's all about telling those mature stories, and that means no cartoon villains running around, doing naughty things because they're just a bit mean. No no, they're afraid of their own deaths, and will do anything to prevent it, even rip out human souls or deny other's access to basic life necessities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26053-theantisanta","name":"TheAntiSanta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26053_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}